-The **machine list** listens on one fleet-wide channel
-(`/machines/live/ws`, `machine.view`), rung when a machine's update
-availability changes and when a machine's reachability actually flips
-(not on every reachability tick). The message says only the kind, never
-which machine, so it needs no per-machine scope check; `live-fleet.js`
-then re-fetches the page and swaps its `#machine-results` block, keeping
-ticked checkboxes and the bulk bar — a bulk "Check for updates" fills in
-as each machine finishes (bursts coalesced, at most every 5 s).
+**Fleet pages** listen on one fleet-wide channel (`/machines/live/ws`,
+`machine.view`), rung when a machine's update availability changes, when
+a machine's reachability actually flips (not on every reachability tick)
+and when a Docker job finishes (0.135.0+). The message says only the
+kind, never which machine, so it needs no per-machine scope check.
+`live-fleet.js` then re-fetches the page and swaps each block marked
+`data-live-fleet`, only for the kinds that block lists in
+`data-live-kinds` (`data-live-url` names another source to fetch):
+
+| Page | Block | Refreshed on |
+|---|---|---|
+| Machines | the list | reachability, updates |
+| Dashboard (0.135.0+) | the machine cards (from `/fleet/cards`) | reachability, updates |
+| Docker → Containers (0.135.0+) | the containers table | a finished Docker job |
+| Docker → Settings (0.135.0+) | the machines table | a finished Docker job |
+
+Ticked checkboxes and the bulk bar are kept, a block isn't swapped while
+you type in it or have its row menu open, and bursts are coalesced (at
+most every 5 s) — a bulk "Check for updates" fills in as each machine
+finishes.
